    <statement><p>If a ball is thrown straight up into the air with an initial
velocity of <m>100</m> ft/s, its height in feet after <m>t</m>
second is given by <m>y = {100}t - 16t^2</m>.  Find the average
velocity (include units, ) for the time period beginning when <m>t = 2</m> seconds and lasting</p>
<p>(i) <m>0.5</m> seconds</p>
<p>Average velocity:<fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(ii) <m>0.1</m> seconds</p>
<p>Average velocity:<fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(iii) <m>0.01</m> seconds</p>
<p>Average velocity: <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>Finally based on the above results, guess what the instantaneous
velocity of the ball is when <m>t =2</m>.</p>
<p>Average velocity: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>28\ {\textstyle\frac{\rm\mathstrut ft}{\rm\mathstrut s}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
